                        "sense_id": "500fcb28-854e-3d0e-8529-c2ed0a6448f7",
                        "entry_id": "f1e6f08b-94e5-3b78-b522-859c23967d69",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Danse lente en trois temps, originaire de la Bohême et combinant la valse et la mazurka."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "322ff1e3-48a3-4a1f-9ecf-70e3ab727554",
                                "sense_id": "500fcb28-854e-3d0e-8529-c2ed0a6448f7",
                                "text": "Maintenant, mesdemoiselles, en avant la rédowa."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6f786965-823d-3357-b859-1069e244dd44",
                        "entry_id": "f1e6f08b-94e5-3b78-b522-859c23967d69",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Air sur lequel on exécute cette danse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "metonymically"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ce7b871-5a2b-4f3a-b39d-89349e02c358",
                                "sense_id": "6f786965-823d-3357-b859-1069e244dd44",
                                "text": "La brise, elle, chante un air si pimpant qu'on dirait la première redowa du nouvel empire."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4ccd533e-c2bb-4daa-884d-211ee6e2d909",
                        "source_entry_id": "f1e6f08b-94e5-3b78-b522-859c23967d69",
                        "target_lang_word": "Redowa",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "75813742-fa3b-4b7b-b29a-3da6106a7d06",
                        "source_entry_id": "f1e6f08b-94e5-3b78-b522-859c23967d69",
                        "target_lang_word": "redowa",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "redowa",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "318ff819-d22d-31dc-952d-c9fb52eec85f",
                                        "entry_id": "bf600d1c-2481-3ad7-b150-d48283fe3e21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dance of Czech origin with turning, leaping waltz steps."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16ea0be1-6288-4932-9e2c-44a3575f07bd",
                                                "sense_id": "318ff819-d22d-31dc-952d-c9fb52eec85f",
                                                "text": "The Redowa or Pas de Basque was originally adapted to Polka-Mazurka music, and, consequently, was danced much slower than it is at present, adapted as it is to waltz and galop music. Hence the name Polka-Redowa: — Polka step, Redowa time."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83164080-5cba-4357-a36f-0f338713cdf4",
                                                "sense_id": "318ff819-d22d-31dc-952d-c9fb52eec85f",
                                                "text": "\"The Varsouvienne,\" says one reference, \"apparently originated in France about 1853, in imitation of the Polish Mazurka, Polka, and Redowa."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e64a7f72-8e41-4f7a-8bbc-42d35a3bd68c",
                                                "sense_id": "318ff819-d22d-31dc-952d-c9fb52eec85f",
                                                "text": "The redowa had some popularity in Paris about the year 1845 but in England it was more talked about than danced."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4de7068-3cec-4b85-9aac-245ffb645439",
                                                "sense_id": "318ff819-d22d-31dc-952d-c9fb52eec85f",
                                                "text": "Both Martínez and Jiménez recorded prolifically, usually dance music—the ubiquitous polka as well as such universal favorites as redowas and schottisches."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1d488f1-4f1c-435d-93ba-123a3f042bba",
                                                "sense_id": "318ff819-d22d-31dc-952d-c9fb52eec85f",
                                                "text": "It was imperative also for the social-minded pioneers to learn the styling and to know how to do the different dance steps required during a five- or six-figure cotillion or lancers. The dance steps included the polka, waltz, mazurka, redowa (two-step), and minuet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03283347-7aae-3ff5-b765-5e6feaa1745f",
                                        "entry_id": "bf600d1c-2481-3ad7-b150-d48283fe3e21",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The music for this kind of dance, usually in quick triple time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
